			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				54,
				7
			],
			"Message": "style(Worker): Reformat ESBuild configuration files for consistency\n\nExpand multi-line formatting in Configuration/ESBuild/Target.js and Configuration/ESBuild/Worker.js to improve readability. Apply the same formatting pattern to Source/Configuration/ESBuild/Worker.js for consistency between source and generated outputs.\n\nChanges include:\n- Breaking the __name function call across multiple lines in Target.js\n- Expanding boolean expressions (On, Clean) to multi-line format\n- Adjusting import statements and object properties to multi-line\n\nRebuilt all target files to reflect configuration formatting changes:\n- Target/Worker.js\n- Target/Worker/CSS/Load.js\n- Target/Worker/Policy.js\n- Target/Worker/Register.js\n\nNo functional changes.",
			"SHA": "0ed481ed13c1770d8cd7bb3fdb7483b7f9a40110"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T05:12:03Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				54,
				7
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Worker): Simplify ESBuild target configuration structure\n\nRefactor Configuration/ESBuild/Target.js to use direct variable assignment and named exports instead of arrow function wrapping. The target configuration was simplified for cleaner module output while maintaining identical build behavior.\n\nConfiguration/ESBuild/Worker.js was removed as a redundant intermediate file since Source/Configuration/ESBuild/Worker.js serves as the canonical source. All target files were rebuilt to reflect the configuration changes.",
			"SHA": "cb7efdd7c4e9e64c32be4ccae0ecd15ce1e1f7a0"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T04:06:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				54,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Worker): Use POSIX-compliant sh shebang in build scripts\n\nReplace bash-specific shebang with POSIX-compliant sh in Worker build scripts for improved cross-platform compatibility. Changed:\n- Source/Run.sh: #!/usr/bin/env bash → #!/usr/bin/env sh\n- Source/prepublishOnly.sh: #!/usr/bin/env bash → #!/usr/bin/env sh\n\nThe POSIX sh shell is more universally available across different Unix-like systems (Linux, macOS, BSD) and ensures consistent behavior without requiring bash as a dependency.",
			"SHA": "34f5d0f4366a191fd0264590b1553bea41b1d7f4"
		},
